cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Stress-line ribs versus optimised thickness for buckling of a thin concrete shell floor under combined gravity and sway"
abstract: >-
  A fixed-volume comparison of a uniform 60 mm form-found concrete shell, a dense rib grid,
  three principal-stress-line rib layouts and a zonally optimised thickness, scored by the
  linear buckling factor under gravity plus 0.2 g sway in the worst direction, with a
  geometrically nonlinear imperfection check, a volume sweep and IFC4/DXF exports.
authors:
  - family-names: "Hasib"
    given-names: "Syed Nafiz Reja"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-7162-7890"
repository-code: "https://github.com/syednafizreja/stress-line-ribs-shell-buckling"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-11-17"
keywords:
  - thin shell
  - buckling
  - stress lines
  - ribbed shell
  - CalculiX
  - embodied carbon
